          },
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "t3_detect"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_4_link_two_viewpoints",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Link the views with a line-of-sight sweep",
          "description": "Connect the two perspectives. A line drawn from Earth through Mars to the background stars sweeps eastward during Mars\u2019s normal motion. When Earth begins to overtake Mars, the sweep reverses, and Mars\u2019s apparent position retraces the retrograde path. After Earth passes Mars, the sweep resumes eastward."
        },
