        "id": "step_5_compare_outer_planets",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Compare retrograde loop sizes (Mars vs. Jupiter vs. Saturn)",
          "description": "Return to the heliocentric comparison. Step through retrograde events for different outer planets and observe loop size: Mars is largest, Jupiter is smaller, and Saturn is smallest. The farther the planet, the smaller the apparent angular change produced by Earth\u2019s overtaking geometry."
        },
