        "id": "step_6_recap",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Recap: what you just learned",
          "description": "Review the core ideas: (1) Mars appears to drift east, reverse into a short westward loop, then drift east again; (2) the geocentric epicycle model can reproduce the loop but needs tuned parameters; (3) the heliocentric model explains retrograde motion as Earth overtaking a slower outer planet; (4) a line-of-sight geometry links the night-sky view to the outside view."
